                  "description": "Beeshazari Lakes lie in the buffer zone of Chitwan National Park, a World Heritage Site, Central, Nepal. This wetlands area is part of the Bharandabhar biological corridor, is of international importance. This is a typical oxbow lake system of the sub-tropical inner terai Nepal, which serves as a linkage between Chitwan National Park in the South and Mahabharat hills up to Annapurna mountain range in the North. This lake has been listed in the Ramsar site since 2003. The lake is 7.2 km south of East-West highway, provides excellent habitat conditions as water hole and corridor for endangered and rare wild animals."
